# VPC Peering # 
Hey guys, in this lesson, we're going to configure VPC peering.We'll have VPC'S in two different AWS regions within the same account.
So it's gonna look like this. We've got us-east-1 and us-west-1.We'll have an instance and a VPC
in each of the regions and it's going to set up the security groups and rules,but we need to actually create the VPC peering connection as
well and then do some testing and check what we can do in terms of utilizing those ports and protocols.

# Steps:
1. Downlao0d the YML file from GitHub 
In the file just copy the AMI ID from EC2 launch instance and put the AMI ID on both file (for us-east-1 AMI ID is diifernce and from us-west-1 AMI id is differnce)
2. Then go to cloud formation --> Click on "Create Stack" (With New Resources)--> Choose "Template is ready" --> Select "Upload a template file" --> Then click on "Chose File" --> upload the file (us-east-1)-> Click on "Next" --> Give a Stack name (I put vpc-ppering-lab)-->Click on "Next" --> Click though until we get "Submit" 
