## Do VPC Peering 
1. Open VPC at us-east and us-west 
2. From us-east-1 in LHS under VPC you can see "Peering connection" --> Click on "Create peering connection" --> Put name of the connection my case (my-vpc-n-callifornia)--> Select VPC ID--> Select the VPC which was created during "Create Stack" --> Select another VPC {It can be same account bit different region},select us-west-1(N.Califirnia)--> Select the VPC ID from US-west-1(N.Califirnia)--> Put that ID --> Click "Create Peering Connection" 
3. Now pop over to N.Califirnia (US-East-1)--> Under Peering Connection --> You can see one peering connection wating for acceptence --> Select on "Action" --> Click on "Accept Request" 
Now we have peering connection 
4. Now we need a Route table beacuse we can route between this two VPC 

## Create Route Table 
1. Under US-East-1(N.California) --> Click on route tables --> Find teh route table for the specific VPC --> Select the exact route table --> Then under Route tab --> Click on Edit --> Add Route --> Put the CIDR block for opposite VPC (10.0.0.0/16) --> Target (Peering connection)--> Click on "Save Change"

2. Now come to US-Wst-1(N.Verginia) --> Under Route Tables --> Find the route tables --> Under Rote tab --> Click on Edit --> Add Routes --> Put Destination (10.1.0.0/16) --> Target "Peering connection" --> Click on "Save"

Now we have VPC Peering connection , Routing bidirectionally 

